  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: High temperatures throughout Northern \nNevada Monday afternoon will be around five degrees above normal \nfor this time of year. This will result in a moderate risk of \nheat-related illnesses. \n\nThe anticyclone aloft will move into the South Central United \nStates Monday through Wednesday. This will push monsoonal moisture\nnorthward into most of Northern and Central Nevada, resulting in \nscattered showers and thunderstorms each afternoon and evening \nMonday through Wednesday. The primary thunderstorm hazards will \nbe localized flooding, small hail, wind gusts near 45 mph, and \ndangerous cloud to ground lightning strikes. Here are \nthunderstorm probabilities for select locations in Eastern Nevada \non Tuesday, July 21st, 2026:\n\nEly - 50% \nLund - 50%\nGreat Basin National Park - 50%\nEureka - 48%\nCurrie - 45%\nRuby Lake - 43%\nAustin - 41%\nElko - 36%\nWells - 36%\nWest Wendover - 31%\n\nMonsoonal moisture should shift eastward Thursday and Friday, but\nlingering thunderstorm chances (slight) will remain in the service\narea forecast. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence\nregarding a moderate risk of heat-related illnesses in Northern\nNevada Monday afternoon. Moderate forecast confidence regarding a\nmarginal risk of excessive rainfall in most of Northern and \nCentral Nevada each afternoon and evening Monday through \nWednesday. High forecast confidence regarding a few strong \nthunderstorms in most of Northern and Central Nevada each \nafternoon and evening today through at least Wednesday. No \ndeviations from the NBM model output.",
